<p class="copy">
	Strange in appearance, carriers are skeletal vessels more akin to the much smaller <?php echo sf_lore_link('trucks', 'trucks'); ?> than the other ships of their size. Carriers are assemblages of structural steel, cabling, and enormous manipulator arms, arrayed concentrically around a core of thrusters and aether sails. Their purpose is to lash together other ships and provide safe transportation while offering rest and repair facilities.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	Civilian carriers ply the aether along standard routes, acting as a form of bulk transportation for other vessels. Military carriers have a more specialized role as mobile ports of call, providing temporary shore leave alongside refit and resupply facilities. In this role, a carrier may be seen cramped between three <?php echo sf_lore_link('frigates', 'frigates'); ?>, or even wrapped like the tentacles of a great beast around a <?php echo sf_lore_link('cruisers', 'cruiser'); ?>.
</p>
